cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  oracle-adaptive: trajectory-aware truncation-degree allocation for lunar
  gravity propagation
message: >-
  Work in progress. The manuscript is a draft whose numerical values are
  placeholders, and no campaign result has been produced yet. Please cite the
  repository rather than any number in it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ayberk
    family-names: Demirkanat
    affiliation: Istanbul Technical University
repository-code: "https://github.com/ayberkdt/oracle-adaptive"
abstract: >-
  Choosing a spherical-harmonic truncation degree over an orbit under a
  quadratic work budget, when the objective takes its norm after a signed
  integral against the state-transition matrix. The coupling matrix depends on
  the epoch pair only through max(i,k), which keeps a full sweep linear in the
  number of accumulation samples and admits a Frank-Wolfe bound on the
  convex-hull relaxation. The repository holds the plan, the pre-registrations,
  the draft, and the campaign code.
keywords:
  - astrodynamics
  - spherical harmonics
  - lunar gravity
  - trajectory optimisation
  - model fidelity
